text: ['({T}: Add {B}.)', '({T}: Add {G}.)', '({T}: Add {R}.)', '({T}: Add {U}.)', '({T}: Add {W}.)', 'All creatures able to block target creature this turn do so.', "As an additional cost to cast this spell, sacrifice a creature.\\nFinal Strike deals damage to target opponent or planeswalker equal to the sacrificed creature's power.", 'As an additional cost to cast this spell, sacrifice a green creature.\\nSearch your library for a green creature card, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', 'Bee Sting deals 2 damage to any target.', "Black creatures you control can't be blocked this turn except by black creatures.", 'Blaze deals X damage to any target.', "Cast this spell only during the declare attackers step and only if you've been attacked this step.\\nCreatures you control gain reach until end of turn. (They can block creatures with flying.)", "Cast this spell only during the declare attackers step and only if you've been attacked this step.\\nDestroy target nonblack attacking creature.", "Cast this spell only during the declare attackers step and only if you've been attacked this step.\\nPrevent all damage that would be dealt to you this turn by attacking creatures.", "Cast this spell only during the declare attackers step and only if you've been attacked this step.\\nReturn one or two target attacking creatures to their owner's hand.", "Cast this spell only during the declare attackers step and only if you've been attacked this step.\\nScorching Winds deals 1 damage to each attacking creature.", "Cast this spell only during the declare attackers step and only if you've been attacked this step.\\nTarget creature gets +1/+3 until end of turn. Untap that creature.", "Cast this spell only during the declare attackers step and only if you've been attacked this step.\\nThis turn, whenever an attacking creature deals combat damage to you, it deals that much damage to its controller.", "Charging Rhino can't be blocked by more than one creature.", 'Counter target creature or sorcery spell.', "Craven Giant can't block.", "Craven Knight can't block.", "Creatures and lands target opponent controls don't untap during their next untap step.", 'Creatures you control get +0/+3 until end of turn.', 'Creatures you control get +1/+1 until end of turn.', "Deep-Sea Serpent can't attack unless defending player controls an Island.", "Defender (This creature can't attack.)", "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\nFlying", 'Destroy all Islands.', 'Destroy all Plains.', 'Destroy all creatures and lands.', "Destroy all creatures. They can't be regenerated.", 'Destroy all green creatures.', 'Destroy all lands.', 'Destroy all white creatures.', 'Destroy target creature or land.', 'Destroy target creature. Its owner gains 4 life.', 'Destroy target land.', 'Destroy target nonblack creature.', 'Destroy target tapped creature.', 'Destroy two target lands.', 'Destroy two target nonblack creatures. You lose 5 life.', 'Draw a card for each tapped creature target opponent controls.', 'Draw four cards. You lose half your life, rounded up.', 'Draw two cards.', 'Dry Spell deals 1 damage to each creature and each player.', "During target player's next turn, creatures that player controls attack you if able.", 'Each player discards any number of cards, then draws that many cards.\\nDraw a card.', 'Each player draws X cards.', 'Each player may draw up to two cards. For each card less than two a player draws this way, that player gains 2 life.', 'Each player shuffles the cards from their hand into their library, then draws that many cards.', 'Earthquake deals X damage to each creature without flying and each player.', 'Fire Tempest deals 6 damage to each creature and each player.', "Fleet-Footed Monk can't be blocked by creatures with power 2 or greater.", 'Flying', "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)", 'Flying, haste', 'Flying, vigilance', 'Flying\\nCloud Dragon can block only creatures with flying.', 'Flying\\nCloud Pirates can block only creatures with flying.', 'Flying\\nCloud Spirit can block only creatures with flying.', "Flying\\nWhen Alabaster Dragon dies, shuffle it into its owner's library.", 'Flying\\nWhen Dread Reaper enters the battlefield, you lose 5 life.', 'Flying\\nWhen Ebon Dragon enters the battlefield, you may have target opponent discard a card.', 'Flying\\nWhen Fire Dragon enters the battlefield, it deals damage to target creature equal to the number of Mountains you control.', "Flying\\nWhen Ingenious Thief enters the battlefield, look at target player's hand.", 'Flying\\nWhen Owl Familiar enters the battlefield, draw a card, then discard a card.', "Forestwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Forest.)", 'Forked Lightning deals 4 damage divided as you choose among one, two, or three target creatures.', "Green creatures you control gain forestwalk until end of turn. (They can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Forest.)", 'Haste', 'Haste (This creature can attack and {T} as soon as it comes under your control.)', 'Haste (This creature can attack and {T} as soon as it comes under your control.)\\nWhen Thundermare enters the battlefield, tap all other creatures.', "Hulking Cyclops can't block.", "Hulking Goblin can't block.", 'Hurricane deals X damage to each creature with flying and each player.', 'If an opponent controls more lands than you, search your library for up to three Plains cards, reveal them, put them into your hand, then shuffle.', 'If target opponent has more cards in hand than you, draw cards equal to the difference.', "Islandwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls an Island.)", "Jungle Lion can't block.", 'Lava Axe deals 5 damage to target player or planeswalker.', "Look at target opponent's hand.\\nDraw a card.", "Look at the top five cards of target opponent's library. Put one of those cards into that player's graveyard and the rest on top of their library in any order.", 'Look at the top seven cards of your library. Put two of them into your hand and the rest into your graveyard.', 'Look at the top three cards of your library, then put them back in any order. You may shuffle.\\nDraw a card.', "Mountainwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Mountain.)", 'Needle Storm deals 4 damage to each creature with flying.', "Phantom Warrior can't be blocked.", "Put target creature on top of its owner's library.", 'Pyroclasm deals 2 damage to each creature.', 'Reach (This creature can block creatures with flying.)', 'Return target card from your graveyard to your hand.', 'Return target creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield.', 'Return target creature card from your graveyard to your hand.', "Return target creature to its owner's hand.\\nDraw a card.", 'Return target sorcery card from your graveyard to your hand.', "Sacred Knight can't be blocked by black and/or red creatures.", 'Scorching Spear deals 1 damage to any target.', 'Search your library for a Forest card, put that card onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', 'Search your library for a basic land card, put that card onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', 'Search your library for a card, then shuffle and put that card on top. You lose 2 life.', 'Search your library for a creature card, reveal it, then shuffle and put that card on top.', 'Search your library for a sorcery card, reveal it, then shuffle and put that card on top.', 'Soul Shred deals 3 damage to target nonblack creature. You gain 3 life.', 'Spitting Earth deals damage to target creature equal to the number of Mountains you control.', "Stalking Tiger can't be blocked by more than one creature.", "Swampwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Swamp.)", "Take an extra turn after this one. At the beginning of that turn's end step, you lose the game.", 'Tap all nonwhite creatures.', 'Tap up to three target creatures without flying.', 'Target creature gains flying until end of turn.\\nDraw a card.', 'Target creature gets +2/+0 until end of turn. Burning Cloak deals 2 damage to that creature.', "Target creature gets +3/+3 and gains flying until end of turn. (It can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)", 'Target creature gets +4/+0 until end of turn.', 'Target creature gets +4/+4 until end of turn.', 'Target opponent discards a card at random.', 'Target opponent reveals their hand. You draw a card for each Forest and green card in it.', 'Target opponent reveals their hand. You draw a card for each Mountain and red card in it.', 'Target player discards two cards.', 'Target player gains 8 life.', 'Target player skips all combat phases of their next turn.', 'Untap all creatures you control.', 'Vampiric Feast deals 4 damage to any target and you gain 4 life.', 'Vampiric Touch deals 2 damage to target opponent or planeswalker and you gain 2 life.', 'Vigilance', 'Volcanic Hammer deals 3 damage to any target.', "When Endless Cockroaches dies, return it to its owner's hand.", 'When Fire Imp enters the battlefield, it deals 2 damage to target creature.', 'When Fire Snake dies, destroy target land.', 'When Gravedigger enters the battlefield, you may return target creature card from your graveyard to your hand.', "When Man-o'-War enters the battlefield, return target creature to its owner's hand.", 'When Mercenary Knight enters the battlefield, sacrifice it unless you discard a creature card.', 'When Noxious Toad dies, each opponent discards a card.', 'When Pillaging Horde enters the battlefield, sacrifice it unless you discard a card at random.', 'When Plant Elemental enters the battlefield, sacrifice it unless you sacrifice a Forest.', 'When Primeval Force enters the battlefield, sacrifice it unless you sacrifice three Forests.', 'When Serpent Assassin enters the battlefield, you may destroy target nonblack creature.', 'When Serpent Warrior enters the battlefield, you lose 3 life.', 'When Spiritual Guardian enters the battlefield, you gain 4 life.', 'When Thundering Wurm enters the battlefield, sacrifice it unless you discard a land card.', "When Undying Beast dies, put it on top of its owner's library.", 'When Venerable Monk enters the battlefield, you gain 2 life.', 'When Wood Elves enters the battlefield, search your library for a Forest card, put that card onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', 'Whenever Charging Bandits attacks, it gets +2/+0 until end of turn.', 'Whenever Charging Paladin attacks, it gets +0/+3 until end of turn.', 'Whenever Seasoned Marshal attacks, you may tap target creature.', 'Whenever Thing from the Deep attacks, sacrifice it unless you sacrifice an Island.', 'White creatures get +2/+0 until end of turn.', 'You gain 1 life for each Forest on the battlefield.', 'You gain 2 life for each Mountain target opponent controls.', 'You gain 3 life for each black creature target opponent controls.', 'You gain 3 life for each creature attacking you.', 'You gain 4 life.', 'You may play up to three additional lands this turn.', '{T}: Capricious Sorcerer deals 1 damage to any target. Activate only during your turn, before attackers are declared.', '{T}: Destroy target tapped creature. Activate only during your turn, before attackers are declared.', '{T}: Target creature gets +2/+2 until end of turn. Activate only during your turn, before attackers are declared.']
flavor: ['"\'O miserable of happy! Is this the end Of this new glorious world . . . ?\'"\\n—John Milton, *Paradise Lost*', '"\'Twas when the seas were roaring With hollow blasts of wind . . . ."\\n—John Gay, "The What D\'Ye Call It"', '". . . [B]efore honor is humility."\\n—*The Bible*, Proverbs 15:33', '". . . inviting the soul to wander for a spell in abysses of solitude . . . ."\\n—Kate Chopin, *The Awakening*', '"As equal were their souls, so equal was their fate."\\n—John Dryden, "Ode to Mrs. Anne Killigrew"', '"As flies to wanton boys, are we to the gods. They kill us for their sport."\\n—William Shakespeare, *King Lear*', '"For he on honey-dew hath fed,\\nAnd drunk the milk of Paradise."\\n—Samuel Taylor Coleridge, "Kubla Khan"', '"Hear that? No? *That\'s* a cat warrior."', '"Hesitation is for the faithless. My belief lends me speed."', '"I am that merry wanderer of the night."\\n—William Shakespeare,\\n*A Midsummer Night\'s Dream*', '"I say victory is better than honor."', '"If it has wings, shoot it. If it doesn\'t, shoot it anyway."', '"Join the army, see foreign countries!" they\'d said.', '"Life can never be *too* good."', '"No bird soars too high, if he soars with his own wings."\\n—William Blake, *The Marriage of Heaven and Hell*', '"No flame, no horror can sway me from my cause."', '"The best armor is to keep out of range."\\n—Italian proverb', 'A fist of dust to line your throat, a bowl of sand to fill your belly.', 'A peasant can do more by faith than a king by proclamation.', 'A rested mind is the sharpest weapon.', 'A rhino rarely uses its horn to announce its charge, only to end it.', 'A thousand feathers from a thousand birds, sewn with magic and song.', 'A touch, not comforting, but of death.', "A true warrior's thoughts are of victory, not death.", "Acting on one good idea is better than hoarding all the world's knowledge.", 'All must fall, and those who stand highest fall hardest.', 'Anyone can get around a cyclops, but few can stand in its way.', 'Are merfolk humans with fins, or are humans merfolk with feet?', 'Asked how it survived a run-in with a bog imp, the pegasus just shook its mane and burped.', "At the sight of the thing the calamari vendor's eyes went wide, but from fear or avarice none could tell.", 'Bitter as wormwood, sweet as mulled wine.', 'Brute force wins the battles. Conviction wins the wars.', "Cast the weight as though it were a die, to see a rival's fate.", 'Chaos does not choose its enemies.', 'Charging alone takes uncommon daring or uncommon stupidity. Or both.', 'Charm and grace may hide a foul heart.', "Come to these woods and suffer no pain; you've burdens to lose and new life to gain.", 'Dawn brings a new day, and a new day brings hope.', 'Death claims all but the darkest souls.', 'Do not react; anticipate.', "Don't be fooled by their looks. Think of them as little knives with wings.", "Don't let its appearance frighten you. Let its claws and teeth do that.", "Don't worry about provoking grizzly bears; they come that way.", 'Doom rarely smells this sweet.', 'Drakes claim to be dragons—until the dragons show up.', 'Dry grass is tinder before the spark.', 'Elves know where to harvest the best of the forest, for they planted it themselves.', 'Energy is never lost, only transformed.', 'Fear is as effective a weapon as the blade.', 'Fire never dies alone.', 'Hill giants are mostly just big. Of course, that does count for a lot!', 'His presence brings not only a strong arm but also renewed hope.', 'Hope is born within.', 'I cast a thousand tiny suns—\\nBeware my many dawns.', 'I howl my soul to the moon, and the moon howls with me.', 'Infantry deployment is the art of putting your troops in the wrong place at the right time.', 'It has more teeth than fit in its mouth.', 'It is not the absence of fear that makes a warrior, but its domination.', 'It moved through the troops leaving no footprints, save on their souls.', 'It pelts the land with its fury, spoiling what was once sweet.', 'It would be a shame to let life slip away to nothing.', "It's easy to stand head and shoulders over those with no backbone.", "It's hard to say for certain which end is more dangerous.", "It's not always gold the thief is after.", "It's not far into the trap, as the crow flies.", "It's up to you if you enter their woods—and up to them if you leave.", 'Its spear has no shaft, its shield no handle.', 'Let the unjust avert their faces and contemplate their peril.', 'Lift your spear as you might lift your glass, and toast your enemy.', 'Like the tide, time both ebbs and flows.', 'Mountaineers quickly learn to travel with their spears always pointed up.', 'Mutual consent is not required for war.', "Nature's secrets can be read on every tree, every branch, every leaf.", 'Never doubt a dragon just because of its size.', 'No one is happy when they notice a tiger.', 'Not all shadows are cast by light—some are cast by darkness.', 'Once they learn the trick of carrying their own lamps, they never touch the ground again.', 'One chill blast—the exhalation of the grave.', "One of the forest's best protectors is the forest itself.", 'Only the heroic and the mad follow mountain goat trails.', 'People ran as never before at the thought of being buried and cremated at the same time.', 'Sailors fear the deep-sea serpent; others thank the gods it has no legs.', "Seafarers fear sailing off the world's edge not so much as down its gullet.", 'Sharper than wind, lighter than air.', 'Some cats are born fighters; others need a little persuading.', 'Some fight for honor and some for gold, but the militia fights for hearth and home.', 'Some fishers like to eat eels, and some eels like to eat fishers.', 'Some think that dryads are the dreams of trees.', 'Something soft bumped against the rowboat, then was gone.', 'Stand in the way of truth at your peril.', 'Stars are like coins dropped into the night: their light buys safe passage.', 'Stay alert: his lumbering may shake the ground itself, but in water, he glides.', 'Storm crow descending, winter unending. Storm crow departing, summer is starting.', 'Summer sends its kiss with warmth and blooming life.', 'Swing your axe as a broom, to sweep away the foe.', 'The bigger they are, the harder they avoid work.', 'The difference between a nuisance and a threat is often merely a matter of numbers.', 'The dogs of war are nothing compared to the cats.', 'The earth cannot hold that which magic commands.', "The fear in their victims' eyes is their most cherished reward.", "The heart's courage is the soul's guardian.", "The herd's patience, the stampede's fury.", 'The less flesh there is, the more teeth there seem to be.', "The lion's only loyalty is to its hunger.", "The more you pay for the lesson, the better you'll remember it.", 'The only thing worse than a minotaur with an axe is an angry minotaur with an axe.', 'The past is a mirror of the future.', 'The phantom warrior comes from nowhere and returns there just as quickly.', "The snake's final thrashings only spread the fire within it.", 'The soldier reaped the profits of peace.', 'The soldiers chopped and chopped, and still the great tree stood, frowning down at them.', 'The wisest man builds his house *behind* the rock.', 'There are few things as motivating as a swarm of bees.', 'There is much talk about the art of creation. What about the art of destruction?', 'They watched as the snake shed layer after layer until only cold bone remained.', 'They were formidable even before they learned the use of weapons.', 'Those who live amid decay must expect scavengers.', 'Though many have come to this place to wash their wounds, the water has never turned red.', 'Though slow-witted and slow-moving, they are quick to anger.', 'To dodge the unerring knife, one must be free of thought.', 'To soar as high as hope, to dive as swift as justice.', "Unicorns don't care if you believe in them any more than you care if they believe in you.", 'What burns the land, boils the seas.', 'What could it have swallowed to grow so large?', 'When emotions rain down, what rivers will be born?', 'When the cat flies and the bird stalks, guard your horses carefully.', 'Winter settles on the land, and the land prays it will wake.']
artist: ['Adam Rex', 'Adrian Smith', 'Alan Rabinowitz', 'Andrew Robinson', 'Bob Eggleton', 'Brian Durfee', 'Charles Gillespie', 'Christopher Rush', 'Colin MacNeil', 'D. Alexander Gregory', 'Dan Frazier', 'Dermot Power', 'DiTerlizzi', 'Donato Giancola', 'Douglas Shuler', 'Eric Peterson', 'Gerry Grace', 'Hannibal King', 'Janine Johnston', 'John Avon', 'John Coulthart', 'John Matson', 'Kaja Foglio', 'Kev Walker', 'Mike Dringenberg', 'Mike Raabe', 'Paolo Parente', 'Pete Venters', 'Phil Foglio', 'Quinton Hoover', 'Randy Gallegos', 'Rebecca Guay', 'Roger Raupp', 'Romas Kukalis', 'Ron Spencer', 'Scott M. Fischer', 'Steve Luke', 'Ted Naifeh', 'Terese Nielsen', 'Tom Wänerstrand', 'Una Fricker', 'William Simpson', 'Zina Saunders']
